{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>וַהֲקִמֹתִי אֶת הַשְּׁבוּעָה</b> (\"and I will establish the oath\"). There is no need for the Holy One, blessed be He, to promise Yitzhak that He will not violate the oath He swore to his father, for He is not a man to relent (I Samuel 15:29), and Avraham has no other descendant who is a covenant-partner of Elohim. And the oath is not conditional, for in the case of Yaakov it was necessary, because of Esav his brother, to say that in him the covenant and his seed would be fulfilled (Genesis 35:12) — not in Esav. And it appears that this statement, \"וַהֲקִמֹתִי אֶת הַשְּׁבוּעָה,\" is itself accounted as an oath, and therefore the Torah always says (Exodus 33:1), \"the land which I swore to Avraham, to Yitzhak, and to Yaakov,\" \"which You swore to them by Yourself\" (Exodus 32:13), for we find no oath to Yitzhak other than this one. And the Holy One, blessed be He, wished to swear to each of the patriarchs, to make known that each one was worthy of having a covenant forged with him, and that the merit of each one should stand before Him together with their seed, for even though the first oath would have sufficed, it is an addition of merit and honor for them. And therefore He said (Leviticus 26:42), \"and I will remember My covenant with Yaakov, and also My covenant with Yitzhak, and also My covenant with Avraham I will remember, and I will remember the land,\" for all of them are covenant-partners of Elohim. And it is possible that in this oath He added for Yitzhak that He would fulfill in him personally the oath which He swore to Avraham his father — that he himself would be a blessing among the nations, as He said to Avraham his father, \"and in your seed all the nations of the earth shall be blessed\" — and the meaning of the verse would be: and I will establish with you the oath which I swore to Avraham your father, for you are a blessing among the nations. And so He further said regarding Yaakov (Genesis 28:14), \"and in you shall all the families of the earth be blessed, and in your seed.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:35:19.816407726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}